      "sourceTextSha256": "f28cb78d2f55632506f088349dff03d562ef1d5286e9a0a524fa15b94db6082a",
      "text": "After breakfast, head to Trelew Airport for your flight to Corrientes.\n\nOn arrival, transfer to Ibera Lodge near the city of Mercedes. The drive takes less than four hours.\n\nSpend four days at **Ibera Lodge** on a full-board basis. The programme includes private or group excursions.\n\nThe Iberá Wetlands cover a vast area of lakes, marshes and islands of vegetation. More than 300 bird species live here. You may also see capybaras, caimans and many other reptiles.\n\nWater lilies, hyacinths and irises cover the water. On higher, drier ground, you’ll find laurels, coral trees, palms and ferns. Marshes, lagoons, patches of jungle and waterfalls make up the reserve’s varied landscape.\n\nAfter the long transfer, settle in at the lodge and start exploring the wetlands close to where you’re staying.",
